1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,140
今天是我们家重要的一天
Okay, big day for this household.

2
00:00:03,140 --> 00:00:05,020
没错 好激动
It certainly is. So exciting.

3
00:00:05,020 --> 00:00:06,300
什么都比不上开始一个新工作
Nothing like starting a new job.

4
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:09,040
或是终于能在已有的工作中充分施展才能
Or finally coming into your own at a job you already have.

5
00:00:09,080 --> 00:00:10,680
新事物带来的美好承诺
The promise of something new.

6
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:12,700
回报终于...
The rewards finally being --

7
00:00:12,760 --> 00:00:14,340
相反的事情却一样地美好
Opposite things being equally good.

8
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:15,820
-干杯 -干杯
- Cheers. - Yes.

9
00:00:15,978 --> 00:00:18,615
我刚接受了一份在CFJ的工作
I have accepted a job at the C.F.J.,

10
00:00:18,615 --> 00:00:20,360
也就是司法中心
The -- the Center For Justice.

11
00:00:20,360 --> 00:00:21,500
不 那其实是一个
Not, it turns out,

12
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:23,100
超级英雄们的秘密总部
a secret headquarters for superheroes.

13
00:00:23,100 --> 00:00:25,037
没有啦 算是吧
No, it -- it kind of is.

14
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:26,680
那是我在法学院的一个朋友
It's a legal-aid society

15
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:28,560
建立的一所司法救援团体
founded by a law-school friend of mine.

16
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:30,840
我将成为人民的律师
I will be an advocate for the people,

17
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:32,700
为无法发言的人发言
a voice for the voiceless.

18
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:34,740
一样重要的是
And just as important...

19
00:00:34,740 --> 00:00:35,597
谢谢
Oh, thank you.

20
00:00:35,597 --> 00:00:38,700
今晚 我将主持"春季叮当嘉年华"
Tonight, I am chaperoning the Spring-A-Ding-Fling,

21
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:40,240
筹款 舞会
a fundraiser, a dance,

22
00:00:40,380 --> 00:00:41,420
在我的带领下
which, under my stewardship,

23
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:43,620
已经打破了学校记录
has shattered school records.

24
00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:45,360
我还加了"叮当"
And I added the "A-ding."

25
00:00:45,414 --> 00:00:47,762
以前一般就叫春季嘉年华
It used to just be called the Spring Fling.

26
00:00:49,260 --> 00:00:50,860
我应该先说我的事情
I should have said my thing first.

27
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:54,140
各位
Hey, guys.

28
00:00:54,740 --> 00:00:57,160
我今晚开场穿这身 说实话
For my opening number tonight -- be honest.

29
00:00:57,160 --> 00:01:00,160
能看出来我在下面穿了别的吗
Does it look like I have anything on under this?

30
00:01:01,060 --> 00:01:02,840
今晚就是SCARB之夜
Tonight is the SCARB.

31
00:01:03,160 --> 00:01:05,680
南加州房地产经纪人年会
Southern California Annual Realtors' Banquet.

32
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:08,420
这是南加州房地产经纪人的盛会
It is the banquet for southern California realtors.

33
00:01:08,600 --> 00:01:09,780
说真的 唯一的盛会
Literally, it's the only one.

34
00:01:09,780 --> 00:01:12,328
而这家伙主持了两次
And this guy is the only two-time host --

35
00:01:12,328 --> 00:01:12,927
三次
Three-time.

36
00:01:13,020 --> 00:01:15,460
三次宴会 史上唯一一人
three-time host in the history of the event.

37
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:17,880
不幸的是 我今年无法参加了
Unfortunately, I have to miss it this year.

38
00:01:18,020 --> 00:01:18,760
这样也好
It's for the best.

39
00:01:18,840 --> 00:01:20,140
她在这种场合总是被无视
She's invisible at these things.

40
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:21,880
嫁给大明星就是这么不容易
It's tough being married to the rock star.

41
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,920
幸运的是 我另找了一个伴侣
Luckily, I lined up a substitute date.

42
00:01:25,420 --> 00:01:26,820
老爸 你还没睡
Dad. You're still up.

43
00:01:26,860 --> 00:01:28,980
是啊 还在想宴会上要讲的段子
Yeah, just working on some jokes for the banquet.

44
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:30,360
你跟我一起去怎么样
Hey, how'd you like to come with me?

45
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:31,760
当然好了
I would love to!

46
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:33,440
她会答应我毫不意外
Not surprised she said yes.

47
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:34,760
那丫头天生懂房产
That girl's got real estate in her blood.

48
00:01:34,820 --> 00:01:36,100
她小时候常常跟着我
She used to come with me to open houses

49
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:36,960
去带客户看房
when she was little.

50
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:38,420
我们甚至还谈过
We may have even talked about

51
00:01:38,420 --> 00:01:39,740
父女档一起合作呢
a father/daughter partnership.

52
00:01:40,540 --> 00:01:42,140
是啊 她最近有些偏离正轨
Yeah, she's been drifting a little lately,

53
00:01:42,140 --> 00:01:43,060
但让她感受一下
but I think a taste

54
00:01:43,060 --> 00:01:45,340
地区房地产经纪人的魅力之夜
of regional real-estate's most glamorous night

55
00:01:45,428 --> 00:01:47,739
也许能重新燃起她的激情
might just re-ignite that flame.

56
00:01:48,260 --> 00:01:50,220
难以置信我居然得去参加这种宴会
I can't believe I have to go to this thing.

57
00:01:50,380 --> 00:01:51,680
但我有什么选择呢
But what choice did I have?

58
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:53,280
我当然愿意
I would love to!

59
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:55,780
但你不会吃饼干不配牛奶吧
But you're not gonna have those cookies without milk, right?

60
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:56,900
对噢
Right.

61
00:01:57,500 --> 00:01:58,600
不给力啊 菲尔
Come on, Phil.

62
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:18,980
休息区
Break area.

63
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:19,840
复印机
Copier.

64
00:02:20,220 --> 00:02:21,120
我的小臭狗
My stinky dog.

65
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:22,980
瞧瞧啊
Oh, look at you.

66
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,080
你刚刚吐了一地
You just threw up recently. Okay.

67
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:26,300
我的天呐
Oh, my gosh.

68
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:27,800
那是你和米歇尔·奥巴马
That's you and Michelle Obama.

69
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:28,780
那是我姨
That's my aunt.

70
00:02:29,060 --> 00:02:30,560
真抱歉
I am so sorry.

71
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:31,580
我不知道我为什么会以为
I don't know why I thought that --

72
00:02:31,580 --> 00:02:32,440
淡定 别有什么白人内疚感
Calm down, white guilt.

73
00:02:32,460 --> 00:02:33,280
那就是米歇尔·奥巴马
It's Michelle Obama.

74
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:34,716
太好了
Oh, good, yeah.

75
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:36,960
是啊 这15年你成就了很多啊
Yeah, you've accomplished a lot in 15 years.

76
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:38,420
在事业上是的
Professionally, yeah.

77
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:40,986
我已经六个月没有约会了
I haven't had a date in six months.

78
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:43,360
有时候周日我会开车去看看我的冷冻卵子
Some sundays, I drive out to visit my frozen eggs.

79
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:45,020
但是从好的一面来说
But, on the plus side,

80
00:02:45,020 --> 00:02:46,880
我跟我妈妈非常亲密
I have gotten really close with my mom.

81
00:02:46,980 --> 00:02:48,660
看那照片 我都看出相似之处了
Oh, look at that. I see the resemblance.

82
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:49,560
那是马娅·安杰卢
That's Maya Angelou.

83
00:02:49,580 --> 00:02:50,100
该死
Damn it.

84
00:02:50,100 --> 00:02:51,040
上面有签名 米奇
It's signed, Mitch.

85
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:52,300
对 我看到了
Yeah. I see that.

86
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:53,540
我们合作会很有意思的
This is gonna be fun!

87
00:02:53,540 --> 00:02:54,260
是啊
I know!

88
00:02:54,260 --> 00:02:55,869
-我真的非常期待 -你
- I'm just really looking for - You!

89
00:02:55,940 --> 00:02:57,440
昨晚那身衣服算怎么回事
What was that outfit last night?

90
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:58,520
那可是商务晚宴
That was a business dinner!

91
00:02:58,540 --> 00:02:59,800
你到底怎么回事
What is wrong with you?

92
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:00,980
温迪 我尽力了
Wendy, I tried.

93
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:02,020
那就更努力一点啊
Well, try harder.

94
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:05,040
这是你的办公室
Ooh, here's your office.

95
00:03:05,240 --> 00:03:05,740
好的
Okay.

96
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:07,320
真不错啊
Oh, this is nice.

97
00:03:07,540 --> 00:03:09,460
是啊 丹尼斯以前也很喜欢
Yeah. Dennis liked it...

98
00:03:09,540 --> 00:03:10,380
后来就不喜欢了
until he didn't.

99
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:11,940
我过会儿再来找你
I'll check on you later.

100
00:03:12,020 --> 00:03:13,180
好 好的
Okay. All right.

101
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:15,820
来看看
Let's see here.

102
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:21,180
新来的吗
New guy?

103
00:03:21,180 --> 00:03:23,120
是啊 你好 我叫米奇尔·普里契特
Uh, yes. Hi. I'm Mitchell Pritchett.

104
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:23,440
我是丹
Dan.

105
00:03:24,020 --> 00:03:25,720
希望你周日晚上没有安排
Hope you don't have any plans for Sunday night.

106
00:03:25,780 --> 00:03:27,940
丹 你怎么还在这里
Dan! What are you still doing here?

107
00:03:28,040 --> 00:03:28,380
快走啊
Go!

108
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:29,200
抱歉
Sorry.

109
00:03:30,020 --> 00:03:30,380
没错
Right.

110
00:03:30,880 --> 00:03:31,580
那边
That way!

111
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:38,540
不是吧
Oh, no.

112
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:45,340
我很喜欢皮革的
I do love it in leather.

113
00:03:45,969 --> 00:03:47,700
那就试着喜欢丝绸的
Well, learn to love it in silk.

114
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:49,720
穿皮革出去太热了
It's too hot outside to be wearing leather.

115
00:03:49,720 --> 00:03:51,624
我是说这辆车
I'm talking about this car.

116
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:52,480
顺便说一句
Oh, by the way,

117
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:54,740
今天去经销商那里 我来讲价
I do the negotiating at the dealership today.

118
00:03:54,900 --> 00:03:55,240
为什么
Why?

119
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:56,620
亲爱的 我是生意人
Honey, I'm a businessman.

120
00:03:56,720 --> 00:03:57,640
跟人打交道
When it comes to people,

121
00:03:57,640 --> 00:03:59,680
我知道该怎么从他们那里得到我想要的
I know how to get what I want out of them.

122
00:04:00,300 --> 00:04:01,020
这块表
This watch --

123
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:03,880
那家伙最后是半价卖给我的
The man sold it to me for half of what he was asking.

124
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:06,700
这鞋 三分之一
These -- a third.

125
00:04:06,848 --> 00:04:09,011
这些 是免费的
These -- for free.

126
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:13,500
你说谁更会说服人 生意人先生
So, who's better at working people, Mr. Businessman?

127
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:14,760
好吧 我们方法不同
Fine. We have different approaches,

128
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:16,020
但我们都很厉害
but we're both pretty good.

129
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:20,040
喂 米奇
Hello, Mitch.

130
00:04:20,700 --> 00:04:21,660
小子
Hey, buddy.

131
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:23,420
你看起来像是要站起来走路啊
You look like you want to get up and walk.

132
00:04:24,840 --> 00:04:25,940
大器晚成 好吧
Late bloomer -- fine.

133
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:27,160
谁在乎别人家的小孩
Who cares if the other kids

134
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:28,257
叫你"慢吞吞的乔"呢
call you "Slo-Joe"?

135
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:30,340
他们就是这样叫你的
And they do, you know.

136
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:31,660
拜拜
Bye-bye.

137
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,040
我们得下次再去买车了
We're gonna have to reschedule the car shopping.

138
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:36,480
米奇得去工作
Mitch has to work.

139
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,469
小卡得去跳舞
Cam has to dance.

140
00:04:37,469 --> 00:04:39,242
我们得照看莉莉
We have to sit Lily.

141
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:40,820
-怎么了 -没啥
- What? - Nothing.

142
00:04:40,843 --> 00:04:42,847
只是...换做我的话就能推掉这件事
Just -- I could have got us out of that.

143
00:04:45,380 --> 00:04:45,740
住手
Stop!

144
00:04:46,085 --> 00:04:47,200
-吃掉 -从我身上下去
- Eat it! - Get off me!

145
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:48,460
吃草吧 牛儿
Eat the grass, cow!

146
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:50,120
-朗达 -您好 邓菲太太
- Hi, Rhonda. - Hi, Mrs. Dunphy.

147
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:50,920
妈妈
Hey, mom.

148
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:52,940
亲爱的 舞会就快开始了
Honey, it's getting very close to time for the dance.

149
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:53,960
你不该进屋去换衣服吗
Shouldn't you go in and get changed?

150
00:04:54,080 --> 00:04:54,760
我已经换了
I did already.

151
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:55,740
他们在来的路上
The guys are coming by.

152
00:04:55,740 --> 00:04:56,800
我们从这里骑车去
We're gonna ride from here.

153
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:57,680
你呢 朗达
What about you, Rhonda?

154
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:59,040
要进屋去把自己弄干净吗
You want to go in and get cleaned up?

155
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:00,120
-我没事 -是吗
- I'm good. - Are you?

156
00:05:00,120 --> 00:05:01,700
你脸上还有泥巴呢
What about that dirt on your face?

157
00:05:01,700 --> 00:05:03,040
卢克 你在这等着
Luke, you wait here.

158
00:05:03,060 --> 00:05:03,940
和你朋友们骑车去
Ride with your friends.

159
00:05:03,940 --> 00:05:05,520
我带朗达去 来吧
I will bring Rhonda. Come on.

160
00:05:07,040 --> 00:05:09,820
进屋之前像狗那样
Just, um, give me a good shake like a dog

161
00:05:09,820 --> 00:05:10,660
好好抖抖身上的泥巴
before you go inside.

162
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:13,420
我就知道
I know.

163
00:05:15,141 --> 00:05:15,960
我爸爸有三处纹身
And my dad has three tattoos.

164
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:17,240
为啥啊 你都是当爹的人了
Like, "Why? You're a dad."

165
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:18,759
父母想要跟上潮流真是太可悲了
Ew! It's so sad when parents try.

166
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:20,160
我妈又在耳朵上打了耳洞
My mom double-pierced one of her ears,

167
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:21,160
我说 拜托
and I'm like, "Hello!

168
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:22,320
您都50了
You're 50."

169
00:05:22,460 --> 00:05:24,760
这把年纪还打耳洞简直老到掉渣
It's so old, like, ancient to have an ear piercing.

170
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:27,040
你俩决定去舞会了吗
Uh, you two decide to go to the dance?

171
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:27,920
是啊 但不是认真地去
Well, yeah, but not really.

172
00:05:28,040 --> 00:05:29,100
-但我们要去 -什么
- But, yeah. - What?

173
00:05:29,400 --> 00:05:30,200
我们要带着讽刺态度过去
We're going ironically

174
00:05:30,260 --> 00:05:32,920
嘲笑所有把这事看得很重的孩子们
to make fun of all the kids who make a big deal out of it.

175
00:05:33,260 --> 00:05:34,820
讽刺个屁啊
"Ironic"? My ass.

176
00:05:34,820 --> 00:05:36,200
艾丽克斯喜欢德鲁
Alex likes Drew.

177
00:05:36,360 --> 00:05:37,680
她只是在打安全牌
She's just playing it safe.

178
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:40,020
有那种鲁莽讨厌的妈妈
Now, there are the pushy, obnoxious moms

179
00:05:40,020 --> 00:05:41,200
喜欢卷入其中
who try and get involved,

180
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:42,740
为他们撮合撮合
nudge them towards one another.

181
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:45,200
我们是好意
We mean well.

182
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:51,980
衬衫不错啊 塔克教练
Fancy shirt, coach Tucker.

183
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:53,880
谢谢 你知道我喜欢说什么
Oh, thank you. You know what I like to say.

184
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:54,500
我可能是教练[二等舱]
I might be coach,

185
00:05:54,560 --> 00:05:55,800
但我坐头等舱
but I travel first class.

186
00:05:57,780 --> 00:05:59,100
你想不想
So, what would you think

187
00:05:59,100 --> 00:06:01,560
在今晚的舞会上致开幕词啊
about giving the opening remarks at the dance tonight?

188
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:03,260
艺术委员会从来没有取得这么大的成就
The arts committee has never made this much,

189
00:06:03,260 --> 00:06:04,420
这全都是因为你
and it's all because of you.

190
00:06:04,420 --> 00:06:07,300
各位 我六个月前来到这所学校时
Oh, you guys, when I came to this school six months ago,

191
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:09,980
从没想到你们会敞开怀抱接纳我
I never would have imagined you would embrace me.

192
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:11,720
抱歉 这里是化学实验室吗
Excuse me? Is this a chem lab?

193
00:06:11,980 --> 00:06:13,460
因为我在期待"大反应"
Because I'm looking for a big reaction.

194
00:06:13,740 --> 00:06:15,100
这就有了
And there it is.

195
00:06:15,100 --> 00:06:16,663
大家好啊
Hi. How are --

196
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:18,960
这位是谁啊
Who is this?

197
00:06:19,064 --> 00:06:21,780
休假过得怎么样
How was sabbatical?

198
00:06:21,780 --> 00:06:22,260
棒极了
Amazing.

199
00:06:22,700 --> 00:06:23,980
我准备好...
I'm rested and ready...

200
00:06:23,980 --> 00:06:25,300
度另一个假了
...to take another vacation.

201
00:06:25,570 --> 00:06:27,688
他怎么称呼啊
And how are we supposed to know him?

202
00:06:27,688 --> 00:06:31,568
卡普兰先生 传奇的西班牙语老师
Senor Kaplan, legendary Spanish teacher.

203
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:34,060
我有点同情他
You know, my heart went out to him a little

204
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:35,780
因为他离开时还是大家的最爱
because he left as everyone's favorite,

205
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:39,440
我敢肯定关于我的消息传出去了
and I'm sure word got out about, you know...me.

206
00:06:40,060 --> 00:06:41,940
我只是不想让他觉得被取代了
I just didn't want him to feel displaced.

207
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:44,180
好了 让一让 大个儿
Okay. Excuse me, big guy.

208
00:06:44,700 --> 00:06:45,700
大家都有礼物哦
Gifts for everyone.

209
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:48,500
安吉拉 这是刚从阿奴拉达普勒带来的
Angela, this is fresh from Anuradhapura.

210
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:49,661
凯伦
And, uh, Karen,

211
00:06:49,661 --> 00:06:52,280
这个要和印度薄饼搭配吃哦
you might want to eat some chapati with that.

212
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:54,120
这是给...
And this is for, um --

213
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:55,011
-她叫玛西亚 -玛西亚
- It's Marcia. - Marcia!

214
00:06:55,020 --> 00:06:56,440
当然啦 我知道的
Right, of course. I knew that.

215
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:58,465
我刚才满脑子肯定都是西班牙语
I must have been having a "Senor" moment.

216
00:06:58,780 --> 00:06:59,760
某人总是如此
Somebody's always on.

217
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:03,240
这是谁干的
Who did this?

218
00:07:03,240 --> 00:07:04,100
出什么事了
What happened?

219
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:05,480
有人把我的包摔到地上
Somebody knocked my bag down

220
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:06,520
摔坏了我的手机
and broke my phone.

221
00:07:06,880 --> 00:07:08,360
莉莉 你知道是怎么回事吗
Lily, do you know anything about this?

222
00:07:08,540 --> 00:07:09,540
他干的
He did it.

223
00:07:10,260 --> 00:07:10,500
乔
Joe.

224
00:07:10,940 --> 00:07:12,200
是啊 我要去玩了
Yep. I'm going to go and play.

225
00:07:13,560 --> 00:07:14,440
她撒谎了
She lies.

226
00:07:14,580 --> 00:07:16,440
乔怎么会把包从桌子上推下去
How could Joe pull a bag off a table?

227
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:17,380
他都不会走路
He can't even walk.

228
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:18,380
我去和她谈谈
I'll talk to her.

229
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:19,020
为什么是你
Why you?

230
00:07:19,320 --> 00:07:21,100
因为你是个知道怎么
Because you're such a businessman

231
00:07:21,100 --> 00:07:22,500
和别人谈话的生意人吗
that knows how to talk to people?

232
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:24,080
相信我 我跟她谈完之后
Trust me. When I get done talking to her,

233
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:26,260
她不但会承认错误
not only will she have confessed to the crime,

234
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:27,860
我还可能卖给她一个橱柜
I might even sell her a closet.

235
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:31,160
我记得有次
I remember my buddies

236
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:32,880
小伙伴们和我在玩石头大战
and I were playing rock war once.

237
00:07:34,220 --> 00:07:34,820
那是个游戏
That's a game

238
00:07:34,820 --> 00:07:36,720
我们把石头丢到对方的脑袋上
where you chuck rocks at each other's heads.

239
00:07:37,620 --> 00:07:38,820
能出什么事啊 对吧
What could go wrong, right?

240
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:41,680
我把一块石头砸到了
I put one through the window

241
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:43,400
我爸漫步者车的窗户上
of my old man's Rambler,

242
00:07:43,980 --> 00:07:46,700
他觉得是我的小弟弟干的
and he thought my baby brother did it.

243
00:07:46,700 --> 00:07:48,080
我无法接受
I couldn't take it,

244
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:50,020
告诉他是我干的
and I told him I did it.

245
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:52,520
坦白的感觉棒极了
It felt so good to confess,

246
00:07:52,820 --> 00:07:54,840
我爸爸很为我感到骄傲
and my old man was so proud of me,

247
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:57,300
我甚至都没被他责罚
I didn't even get in any trouble.

248
00:07:57,322 --> 00:07:59,017
知道吗
Y-you know?

249
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:01,660
是乔干的
Joe did it.

250
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:05,960
她很厉害
She's good.

251
00:08:06,200 --> 00:08:07,000
好好看看 学着点
Watch and learn.

252
00:08:07,060 --> 00:08:08,260
我觉得她不吃你
I don't think that cleavage thing

253
00:08:08,260 --> 00:08:09,220
露乳沟这一套吧
is gonna work with this one.

254
00:08:09,220 --> 00:08:10,480
我又不是只会这一招
That's not my only trick.

255
00:08:11,600 --> 00:08:12,200
好啊 莉莉
Hola, Lily.

256
00:08:12,740 --> 00:08:13,760
外公去哪儿了
Where did grandpa go?

257
00:08:13,860 --> 00:08:14,960
别担心杰
Don't worry about Jay.

258
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:17,020
现在这里只有我和你
It's only you and me here now.

259
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:19,420
告诉我
So, tell me.

260
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:21,660
你最喜欢哪个
Which one of these is your favorite?

261
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:23,280
没关系
Fine.

262
00:08:24,380 --> 00:08:25,080
慢慢来
One by one,

263
00:08:25,080 --> 00:08:26,240
它们都会消失
they will disappear.

264
00:08:27,780 --> 00:08:28,860
或早或晚
Sooner or later,

265
00:08:28,860 --> 00:08:31,040
我们会找到你最爱的那个
we'll get to the one that you love.

266
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:33,700
女士们先生们
Ladies and gentlemen,

267
00:08:33,760 --> 00:08:35,640
他是中介之王
he's the emperor of escrow.

268
00:08:35,651 --> 00:08:38,400
他太棒了
He puts the toot in tooter.

269
00:08:38,400 --> 00:08:40,720
大家鼓掌欢迎
Let's put your hands together for

270
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:43,869
菲尔·邓菲
Phil Dunphy!

271
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:47,480
感谢这么好的司仪
Thanks for the kind introduction,

272
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:48,240
也就是我
me.

273
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:52,400
不像前几年
Now, unlike past years...

274
00:08:52,400 --> 00:08:54,180
我不会再站在这
I'm not gonna stand up here

275
00:08:54,180 --> 00:08:56,020
一直冲你们叽哩呱啦
and talk your ears off.

276
00:08:56,220 --> 00:08:57,420
不 女士们先生们
No, ladies and gentlemen.

277
00:08:58,320 --> 00:08:59,400
应该给你们点好东西
You deserve more.

278
00:09:00,100 --> 00:09:01,080
今年
This year,

279
00:09:01,959 --> 00:09:04,041
我要把词都唱出来
I'm gonna sing them off.

280
00:09:04,060 --> 00:09:07,440
*我要卖*
*I'm selling away*

281
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:13,500
*周六挂出一间房子开卖*
*Set an open house for Saturday*

282
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:18,000
*经纪人们的聚会*
*A gathering of agents*

283
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:20,640
*出现在大篷车*
*Appeared in caravan*

284
00:09:20,640 --> 00:09:27,200
*我刚刚离婚*
*I'm a new divorce*

285
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:29,740
*我现在需要间房子*
*Now I need a house*

286
00:09:29,740 --> 00:09:31,940
*可以让我养猫*
*That's cat-friendly*

287
00:09:34,460 --> 00:09:36,160
人们说伟大的艺术家
They say the greats

288
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:38,100
绝不会让任何事情影响表演
never let anything affect their performance.

289
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,340
或许这些伟人没有女儿
Well, maybe the greats never had a daughter

290
00:09:40,340 --> 00:09:42,120
在你计划好的五次实时台上换装中的
who checked out during the third of five planned

291
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:44,060
第三次时走神
real-time, mid-performance wardrobe changes.

292
00:09:44,778 --> 00:09:45,889
我不得不说
I'm not gonna lie.

293
00:09:46,160 --> 00:09:47,240
这让我丧失了信心
It knocked me off my game.

294
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,240
*在板子上*
*On the board*

295
00:09:53,660 --> 00:09:55,400
这是表演的一部分吗
Is this part of it?

296
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:55,880
不是
No.

297
00:09:56,180 --> 00:09:57,620
这不是表演的一部分
It's not part of it.

298
00:10:03,120 --> 00:10:04,260
在法学院
In law school,

299
00:10:04,340 --> 00:10:06,420
温迪·柯克就有点容易情绪激动
Wendy Kirk could be a little intense.

300
00:10:06,580 --> 00:10:09,040
我一直希望她会越来越温柔 可是
I always hoped that she'd soften over time, but...

301
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:11,800
有些人会向相反方向发展
...some people go the other way.

302
00:10:12,700 --> 00:10:13,740
这地方是个噩梦
This place is a nightmare.

303
00:10:14,180 --> 00:10:15,340
情况很糟糕
The conditions are deplorable,

304
00:10:15,380 --> 00:10:16,600
大家都不应该
and no one should have to suffer

305
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:18,900
每天遭受这样的虐待
this kind of abuse on a daily basis.

306
00:10:19,340 --> 00:10:23,200
什么暴君像这样完全不尊重人命啊
What kind of tyrant has such utter disregard for human life?

307
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:24,400
我干不下去了
I can't do this.

308
00:10:24,740 --> 00:10:25,380
你必须干下去
You have to.

309
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:26,480
温迪需要听到
Wendy needs to hear it.

310
00:10:26,526 --> 00:10:27,840
是啊 可我紧张 要是她
Yeah, but I'm nervous. You know, what if she --

311
00:10:27,840 --> 00:10:29,020
-米奇尔 -是 你好
- Mitchell. - Yes! Hi!

312
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:30,700
我刚刚想到一个好主意
I just had a great idea.

313
00:10:30,900 --> 00:10:34,060
我觉得你最适合培训雷克斯了
I think you would be the perfect person to groom Rex.

314
00:10:34,060 --> 00:10:35,460
什么
E-excuse me?

315
00:10:35,460 --> 00:10:36,860
我只是觉得他真的会
I just think he'd really respond

316
00:10:36,860 --> 00:10:38,160
和你这样的人产生共鸣
to someone like you, you know?

317
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:39,531
你不介意吧
Y-you don't mind, right?

318
00:10:39,531 --> 00:10:41,529
不不 怎么会
Uh, uh, no. No, not at all.

319
00:10:41,540 --> 00:10:42,300
太好了 谢谢
Great. Thanks.

320
00:10:42,340 --> 00:10:43,460
麻烦你过去自我介绍一下吧
Will you go over and introduce yourself?

321
00:10:43,467 --> 00:10:44,080
自我介 好吧
I-intro-- okay.

322
00:10:44,080 --> 00:10:45,260
-好的 -谢谢
- Okay. Yeah. - Thank you.

323
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:50,040
你好 我是米奇尔
Hello. I'm Mitchell.

324
00:10:50,800 --> 00:10:53,220
显然这现在是我的工作了
And, apparently, this is my job now.

325
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:55,160
天呐 你真臭
Oh, god, you smell.

326
00:10:57,960 --> 00:10:59,380
大家都在看我
People are looking at me.

327
00:11:00,260 --> 00:11:02,600
因为你让我把你打扮得很漂亮
That's because you let me make you beautiful.

328
00:11:03,460 --> 00:11:04,820
别瞎说 我漂亮吗
Stop it. Am I?

329
00:11:05,260 --> 00:11:06,460
你很美
Yes, you are.

330
00:11:06,460 --> 00:11:07,620
玩得开心
Have fun.

331
00:11:07,620 --> 00:11:08,897
去吧去吧
Go. Go.

332
00:11:09,820 --> 00:11:10,960
德鲁 你好 德鲁
Drew. Hey, Drew.

333
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:11,840
玩得开心吗
Having fun?

334
00:11:12,012 --> 00:11:14,160
开心 还好吧
"Fun"? Uh...okay.

335
00:11:14,160 --> 00:11:15,840
德鲁 德鲁 听我说
Oh, Drew. Drew, listen.

336
00:11:16,360 --> 00:11:18,920
我和菲尔今晚会很晚才回家
Phil and I are gonna be out really late tonight,

337
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:21,040
所以你开车带艾丽克斯回去时
so there will not be an adult at the house

338
00:11:21,040 --> 00:11:23,500
家里没有大人
when you drop Alex off,

339
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:24,140
知道我什么意思吗
if you know what I mean.

340
00:11:24,140 --> 00:11:25,080
是的 别担心
Yeah, don't worry.

341
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:26,420
我会开车送她回去
I'll, uh-- I'll drop her off,

342
00:11:26,420 --> 00:11:26,960
我不会进屋的
and I won't go in.

343
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:29,280
大房子
Well... big house,

344
00:11:29,460 --> 00:11:31,020
还有 可爱的女儿
you know... cute daughter--

345
00:11:31,220 --> 00:11:33,600
我不反对你送她进门
I would not be opposed to you walking her in,

346
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:34,920
在我们回家前陪着她
keeping her company until we get back.

347
00:11:34,920 --> 00:11:35,600
我刚说了
Like I said,

348
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:37,720
我们很晚才回家
we will not be back until late.

349
00:11:38,140 --> 00:11:39,500
我听明白了 邓菲太太
I hear you, Mrs. Dunphy.

350
00:11:39,940 --> 00:11:40,560
你可以相信我
You can trust me.

351
00:11:40,780 --> 00:11:43,080
不得不相信你啊 因为我们
Well, gonna have to trust you because we have no way

352
00:11:43,080 --> 00:11:44,340
无法知道你会干些什么
of knowing what you're gonna get up to.

353
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:46,260
这样 要是你的车挡在车道上
In fact, if your car is blocking the driveway,

354
00:11:46,260 --> 00:11:47,500
我就鸣两次笛
I'll just honk twice

355
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:48,660
然后等你出来
and wait for you to come out.

356
00:11:48,940 --> 00:11:49,860
-好的 -很好
- Okay. - Okay.

357
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:51,940
去找她吧 小伙子 快去
Go get her, tiger. Come on.

358
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:55,600
干得好 塔克
Nice job, Tucker.

359
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:57,420
你做了很多
I mean, you made so many choices

360
00:11:57,420 --> 00:11:58,720
我不可能做出的选择
that I never would have made,

361
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:00,160
但大部分效果不错
but a lot of them are working.

362
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:01,000
这样啊
Oh, well, you know,

363
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:02,060
我就是看你策划的
I just watched the videos

364
00:12:02,060 --> 00:12:04,280
很多很多舞会视频
of the many, many dances you planned

365
00:12:04,280 --> 00:12:06,345
然后就想出了这么一个主意
and just built off that one on idea.

366
00:12:06,660 --> 00:12:07,580
孩子们
Hey, kids!

367
00:12:07,580 --> 00:12:09,240
我的小甜心们
There are my little chalupas!

368
00:12:13,380 --> 00:12:14,740
你对朗达做了什么
Um, what did you do to Rhonda?

369
00:12:15,020 --> 00:12:15,820
我把她整干净了
I cleaned her up.

370
00:12:15,900 --> 00:12:17,140
不 你毁了她
No, you broke her.

371
00:12:17,220 --> 00:12:18,280
我不喜欢这样的她
I hate her like this.

372
00:12:18,380 --> 00:12:19,560
她美极了
She looks fantastic.

373
00:12:19,560 --> 00:12:20,448
对你来说是
To you!

374
00:12:20,448 --> 00:12:22,680
把她变回去 这样很伤脑筋
Fix her. Ugh, it confuses me.

375
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:23,300
卢克啊
Oh, Luke.

376
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:25,500
"家里没人"
"The house will be empty"?

377
00:12:25,900 --> 00:12:27,360
你在给我拉皮条
You are pimping me out!

378
00:12:27,460 --> 00:12:29,280
你俩显然喜欢对方
It is clear that the two of you like one another.

379
00:12:29,460 --> 00:12:30,600
有时需要有人推你们一把
Sometimes, you need a little nudge.

380
00:12:30,609 --> 00:12:31,740
你可是行为监督人啊
Well, you're a chaperone!

381
00:12:31,740 --> 00:12:32,880
快消失吧
Just disappear!

382
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:34,436
这舞会不是你该来的地方
This dance is not for you!

383
00:12:40,150 --> 00:12:41,405
你真走运 居然是水
You're lucky that's water.

384
00:12:43,051 --> 00:12:44,075
该死
Damn it.

385
00:12:47,660 --> 00:12:49,440
她已经生了一个小时的闷气了
She's been stewing in there for an hour.

386
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:51,160
我们不如锁上门
I say let's lock the door,

387
00:12:51,220 --> 00:12:51,960
拉了电闸
cut the power.

388
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:53,980
让她意识到我们态度有多严肃
Let's show her that we mean business.

389
00:12:54,980 --> 00:12:57,900
我们先采取温和点的手段吧 监狱长
Let's try the joint approach first..."Gitmo."

390
00:13:02,640 --> 00:13:04,620
我们仔细思考了一下你的供词
Okay, we've been going over your story,

391
00:13:04,620 --> 00:13:05,660
不怎么有说服力
and it doesn't add up.

392
00:13:05,700 --> 00:13:07,920
我放包的地方对乔来说太高了
My purse was too high for Joe to reach.

393
00:13:08,260 --> 00:13:10,240
他已经能够着这里了
He's tall enough to reach up here.

394
00:13:10,500 --> 00:13:12,120
他为了拿到我的小动物们
He knocked over the baby powder

395
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:14,680
把婴儿爽身粉碰倒了
trying to get my stuffed animals.

396
00:13:14,860 --> 00:13:15,700
我不信
Not buying it.

397
00:13:15,820 --> 00:13:18,060
看 这还有他走过的脚印呢
Look. You can see the footprints where he walked.

398
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:19,160
走
Walk?

399
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:20,980
莉莉 莉莉 莉莉
Lily, Lily, Lily.

400
00:13:21,100 --> 00:13:22,320
乔还不会走路呢
Joe can't walk.

401
00:13:22,540 --> 00:13:23,720
他在我面前走了
He does for me.

402
00:13:24,100 --> 00:13:26,800
所以你有办法让他走路吗
So, you have ways of making him walk?

403
00:13:28,340 --> 00:13:30,480
莉莉 就承认是你做的吧
Lily, just admit that you did it.

404
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:31,640
过来 乔
Come here, Joe.

405
00:13:32,340 --> 00:13:34,400
像你之前做的那样
Come here like you did before.

406
00:13:34,400 --> 00:13:35,740
宝贝 你在自找难堪
Honey, you're embarrassing yourself.

407
00:13:35,740 --> 00:13:38,014
-过来 乔 -他不会走路
- Come here, Joe. - He can't walk.

408
00:13:40,580 --> 00:13:41,640
他居然会走了
He's walking!

409
00:13:42,160 --> 00:13:44,380
我之前点的那些蜡烛起作用了
The candles that I lit worked!

410
00:13:44,420 --> 00:13:45,640
看他的步子迈得多大
Look at the stride on him.

411
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:47,680
他走得跟山羊一样稳健
He's as surefooted as a mountain goat.

412
00:13:47,680 --> 00:13:48,420
我就说嘛
Told you.

413
00:13:48,720 --> 00:13:51,660
真对不起我们怀疑你了
I'm so sorry that we doubted you.

414
00:13:52,100 --> 00:13:53,540
不敢相信我居然这么幸运
Boy, did I get lucky.

415
00:13:58,380 --> 00:14:00,520
在他学会说话之前
I'm going to blame everything on him

416
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:02,120
他都会是我的替罪羊
until he learns how to talk.

417
00:14:03,460 --> 00:14:05,340
那个男人跳着华尔兹自以为是舞池之王
This guy waltzes in here like he's king of the dance

418
00:14:05,340 --> 00:14:07,620
说什么帮助不发达地区建学校
after doing god knows what in Sri Lanka,

419
00:14:07,620 --> 00:14:09,948
都不知道他在斯里兰卡干了什么勾当
building schools in underdeveloped areas.

420
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:10,920
都不知道他想干嘛
What does that even mean?

421
00:14:10,920 --> 00:14:13,190
你对那个男人是不是有点太苛刻了
Is it possible that you're being a little hard on the man?

422
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:16,700
是我把他的二流舞会办成了年度盛事
I turned his two-bit dance into the event of the year.

423
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:18,300
看 小混混和书呆子
Look. Burnouts and dweebs

424
00:14:18,300 --> 00:14:19,980
能这么和谐共处
hanging out together in harmony.

425
00:14:19,990 --> 00:14:21,213
都是我的功劳
That is me.

426
00:14:21,213 --> 00:14:22,377
我很遗憾 小卡
I'm sorry, Cam.

427
00:14:22,377 --> 00:14:23,520
别替我遗憾
Oh, don't feel sorry for me.

428
00:14:23,520 --> 00:14:25,080
马上就是教职员工舞蹈环节
Next is faculty dance.

429
00:14:25,580 --> 00:14:26,240
卡普兰不会跳舞
Kaplan can't move.

430
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:27,000
都传到Tumblr上了
It's on his Tumblr.

431
00:14:27,200 --> 00:14:28,620
那是他的一大耻辱
It's his big shame.

432
00:14:28,660 --> 00:14:29,420
相信我
Trust me.

433
00:14:29,420 --> 00:14:30,780
他抢不走我的风头
He can't touch this.

434
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:33,690
好了 到了教职员工起舞的时候了
Okay, time now for the faculty dance.

435
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:34,960
老师们 上吧
Go, teachers.

436
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:36,789
你确定吗
Oh, are you sure?

437
00:14:36,789 --> 00:14:39,112
停 现在是小卡秀场
Stop. It's "Cammer" Time.

438
00:14:49,420 --> 00:14:50,580
不介意我也来跳吧 教练
Mind if I join you, coach?

439
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:03,880
休假期间
While on sabbatical,

440
00:15:04,020 --> 00:15:07,140
我在斯里兰卡跟质多斯那学了点舞蹈
I learned a thing or two from Sri Lanka's own Chitrasena.

441
00:15:07,420 --> 00:15:08,820
我不知道他是谁
I don't know who that is,

442
00:15:08,960 --> 00:15:10,600
而且你说话的态度很讨人厌
and it's annoying when you say things

443
00:15:10,600 --> 00:15:12,120
好像谁都应该知道他似的
like people are supposed to know!

444
00:15:12,380 --> 00:15:15,140
看来那个可悲的孔雀男
That pathetic peacock of a man

445
00:15:15,140 --> 00:15:17,100
是要跟我一战到底
was not going down without a fight.

446
00:15:17,920 --> 00:15:19,080
我必须做出选择
I had a choice to make --

447
00:15:19,099 --> 00:15:21,324
要么跳得比他好 要么比他大度
be the better dancer or the bigger man.

448
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:23,140
所以我离开了舞台
So, I stepped off the dance floor

449
00:15:23,140 --> 00:15:24,820
做了最正确的选择
and made the obvious call.

450
00:15:25,320 --> 00:15:26,560
你想吸引大家的注意力吗
You want to win over a crowd?

451
00:15:27,020 --> 00:15:28,520
去邀请一位孤独的母亲共舞吧
Invite a lonely mom to dance.

452
00:15:28,980 --> 00:15:30,140
她没有想到我这一招
She never saw it coming,

453
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:31,320
他也一样
and neither did he.

454
00:15:41,117 --> 00:15:42,417
喂 老兄
Hey Senor.

455
00:15:42,880 --> 00:15:44,260
学着点吧
You just got out-coached.

456
00:15:46,140 --> 00:15:48,260
我尝试看向事物更积极的一面
I try and look on the bright side of things.

457
00:15:48,260 --> 00:15:50,380
我是那种即使要给臭狗洗澡
I-I'm a doggy-bath-is-half-full

458
00:15:50,380 --> 00:15:51,240
也依然乐观的人
kind of guy.

459
00:15:52,020 --> 00:15:53,820
但我应该醒悟了
But it was time for me to open my eyes.

460
00:15:54,700 --> 00:15:56,460
我的老板是个禽兽
I was working for a monster.

461
00:15:56,740 --> 00:15:59,540
我来这里工作是为了替弱势群体说话
I came to this job to be the voice of the downtrodden.

462
00:15:59,740 --> 00:16:02,460
可没想到弱势群体居然就是我的同事
Turns out those downtrodden were my co-workers,

463
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:06,300
他们迫切地需要屠龙的英雄
and they were desperate for a hero to slay their dragon.

464
00:16:07,420 --> 00:16:08,720
各位 不好意思我来晚了
Hey, guys. Sorry I'm late.

465
00:16:08,920 --> 00:16:10,540
雷克斯 你跟米奇尔处得怎么样
Um, Rex, how's it going with Mitchell?

466
00:16:10,680 --> 00:16:11,460
新来的那个吗
The new guy?

467
00:16:11,460 --> 00:16:12,300
我还没见过他呢
I haven't met him yet.

468
00:16:12,480 --> 00:16:14,220
真奇怪 我让他来自我介绍了啊
That's weird. I asked him to introduce himself.

469
00:16:15,320 --> 00:16:16,760
有人看到我的狗了吗
hey, has anybody seen my dog?

470
00:16:17,220 --> 00:16:17,660
皮克希
Pixie!

471
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:19,840
她来了
Oh, there she is.

472
00:16:21,260 --> 00:16:22,240
温迪 不好意思
Okay, Wendy, I'm sorry.

473
00:16:22,240 --> 00:16:23,380
我有话想跟你说
I-I have something to say to you,

474
00:16:23,380 --> 00:16:25,500
一些在座诸位都不敢说的话
something that everybody else here is afraid to say.

475
00:16:25,760 --> 00:16:27,620
我知道你现在做的都是好事
Now, I know you're fighting the good fight,

476
00:16:27,620 --> 00:16:30,000
可是这也不能成为你如此对待别人的借口
but that is no excuse for the way you treat people.

477
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,860
不过这倒有可能导致
T-that actually might be one of the reasons

478
00:16:31,860 --> 00:16:33,020
你没有亲密爱人
that you have no personal life

479
00:16:33,020 --> 00:16:34,340
毕竟谁也不想回家面对
because who wants to come home

480
00:16:34,340 --> 00:16:37,513
一个冷血无情的恶棍
to a-a cold, emotionless...thug?

481
00:16:37,571 --> 00:16:39,100
你 你都在说什么啊
W-what are you talking about?

482
00:16:39,100 --> 00:16:41,420
我是一名经验丰富值得尊重的律师
I am an experienced, respected attorney,

483
00:16:41,420 --> 00:16:42,620
可是上班第一天
and on my first day,

484
00:16:42,620 --> 00:16:44,100
你居然让我去给雷克斯洗澡
you asked me to bathe Rex.

485
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:45,800
我有点无法忍受
I'm not comfortable with that.

486
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:47,360
我也无法忍受
And I'm not comfortable with that,

487
00:16:47,420 --> 00:16:48,320
可我还是做了
but I did it.

488
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:50,120
好吧 那是皮克希
Okay, that's Pixie.

489
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:51,080
这才是雷克斯
This is Rex,

490
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:52,640
我让你培训的实习生
the intern I asked you to groom.

491
00:16:53,420 --> 00:16:54,880
好吧 这是我的错
And that is my mistake,

492
00:16:54,880 --> 00:16:55,920
我负全责
and I own that.

493
00:16:55,960 --> 00:16:57,320
可即使那样
But that is still no excuse

494
00:16:57,320 --> 00:16:58,740
你也没有理由因为他
for the way that you tore into him

495
00:16:58,740 --> 00:17:00,000
昨天的穿着对他大吼大叫
for the outfit he wore yesterday.

496
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:01,980
我当时是为了他给我挑的衣服生气
I was talking about the outfit he picked out for me.

497
00:17:02,100 --> 00:17:04,180
很明显 我招了世界上唯一一个
Apparently, I have the one gay intern in the world

498
00:17:04,180 --> 00:17:05,940
没有时尚嗅觉的男同性恋实习生
with absolutely no fashion sense.

499
00:17:05,940 --> 00:17:07,508
我不了解当时的背景情况
I was unaware of -- of this dynamic.

500
00:17:07,508 --> 00:17:09,510
可是我 我不是一个人 对吧
But I-I-I'm not alone here, all right?

501
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:11,980
这屋里肯定还有别人觉得你是
There are people in this room who feel that you are --

502
00:17:11,980 --> 00:17:13,200
我们应该怎么说呢
How did we say it? --

503
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:16,260
你是个毫不尊重他人的暴君
you are a tyrant with no regard for human life.

504
00:17:16,260 --> 00:17:19,200
听起来像我那个恶房东案子的总结陈词
That sounds like my summation for the slum-lord case.

505
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:20,060
什么 你写完了吗
Oh, hey, you finished it?

506
00:17:20,120 --> 00:17:20,940
写得超棒
It's wonderful.

507
00:17:20,980 --> 00:17:22,340
可是他不好意思给你看
But he's nervous to show you.

508
00:17:22,480 --> 00:17:24,140
你怎么对自己那么苛刻呢
Why are you so hard on yourself?

509
00:17:24,140 --> 00:17:24,822
好吧 那 那么
Okay, but w-w-what --

510
00:17:24,833 --> 00:17:26,922
你强迫我们周日工作又怎么说
what about you making us work on sundays?

511
00:17:26,922 --> 00:17:28,340
是在说 周日晚去我家烧烤吗
That -- the night of my barbecue?

512
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:28,740
丹
Dan?

513
00:17:28,780 --> 00:17:30,120
你怎么还在这里
What are you still doing here?

514
00:17:30,120 --> 00:17:31,980
今天是你的结婚纪念日 快回家
It's your anniversary! Go home!

515
00:17:32,100 --> 00:17:33,520
天哪 告诉我这不是真的
Oh, god. This isn't happening.

516
00:17:33,520 --> 00:17:34,720
不 不 她很疯狂
No, no. She's -- she's crazy.

517
00:17:34,720 --> 00:17:36,260
我看到她攻击自动售货机
I mean, I saw her attack the vending machine.

518
00:17:36,340 --> 00:17:38,500
自从丹尼斯把它弄坏以后就只能那样用了
That's the only way it works since Dennis broke it.

519
00:17:38,660 --> 00:17:40,140
丹尼斯就是之前用我那间办公室的人吗
Dennis is the guy whose office I took?

520
00:17:40,260 --> 00:17:42,360
是的 他曾是那个机器最好的客户
Yeah, he was the machine's best customer

521
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:43,340
直到他开始跑步
until he started running.

522
00:17:43,660 --> 00:17:45,180
有一天他说 他一定要离开 否则
One day, he said he's got to get out or --

523
00:17:45,180 --> 00:17:46,960
他就会死 好吧 好吧
He would die. Okay. Okay.

524
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:47,860
温迪
Wendy, um...

525
00:17:48,120 --> 00:17:49,760
我也许应该向你道歉
I-I might owe you a little bit of an apology,

526
00:17:49,780 --> 00:17:50,440
对不起
so I'm sorry.

527
00:17:51,160 --> 00:17:52,860
很明显 这里每个人都很爱你
Um, clearly, everybody here loves you,

528
00:17:52,860 --> 00:17:54,576
我之前把一切都搞错了
and I-I was wrong about everything.

529
00:17:54,576 --> 00:17:55,612
所以 对不起
So...I'm sorry.

530
00:17:55,612 --> 00:17:58,060
你知道吗 你也不是全搞错了
You know, you -- you weren't wrong about everything.

531
00:17:58,060 --> 00:18:00,700
我虽然拿这事开玩笑 但你是对的
I mean, look, I do joke about it, but you're right.

532
00:18:01,100 --> 00:18:01,700
我孤单一人
I'm alone.

533
00:18:01,780 --> 00:18:04,900
这也不是第一次有人说我冷漠
And that is not the first time that someone has called me cold.

534
00:18:04,900 --> 00:18:06,011
我的那些卵子
Okay, those eggs...

535
00:18:06,500 --> 00:18:07,920
那些卵子取出来就是冷冻的
those eggs came out of me frozen.

536
00:18:08,300 --> 00:18:09,680
而且我还这么高
And I'm impossibly tall.

537
00:18:09,680 --> 00:18:11,580
即使我能找到一个人来爱我
And even if I could find somebody to love me,

538
00:18:11,590 --> 00:18:12,589
他们也够不着啊
they -- they wouldn't be able to reach.

539
00:18:12,599 --> 00:18:13,805
不 别这样
No -- hey, hey. Come on.

540
00:18:13,805 --> 00:18:15,200
你是个很了不起的女性
You're -- you're an amazing woman.

541
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:16,420
她是个了不起的女性
She's an amazing woman.

542
00:18:16,669 --> 00:18:18,360
而且 你是个榜样
And you -- you're a-a role model.

543
00:18:18,360 --> 00:18:19,120
你是个英雄
You're a hero.

544
00:18:19,120 --> 00:18:20,868
我是个六尺高的英雄
I'm a 6-foot hero.

545
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:21,960
不 别这样
No. Come on.

546
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:23,500
你周围的人都爱你
You're surrounded by people who love you.

547
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:25,200
有丹还有雷克斯
Here's Dan and Rex.

548
00:18:25,420 --> 00:18:26,820
还有我 过来
Me. Come here.

549
00:18:26,820 --> 00:18:29,240
还有挂在那里的塞缪尔·杰克逊
All the way up to Samuel L. Jackson there.

550
00:18:30,690 --> 00:18:32,700
那是你妈妈戴着袋鼠牌帽子 是吗
That's your mother in a Kangol hat, isn't it?

551
00:18:32,700 --> 00:18:32,900
是的
Yeah.

552
00:18:33,980 --> 00:18:35,540
你确定你自己在干什么吗 塔德
Um, are you sure you know what you're doing, Tad?

553
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:37,680
我知道你来自抵押医生[机构] 但是
I know you're the Mortgage Doctor, but --

554
00:18:37,680 --> 00:18:38,800
有人问 这里有医生吗
Someone said, "Is there a doctor in the house?"

555
00:18:38,800 --> 00:18:39,800
难道我不应该站出来吗
Was I supposed to not get up?

556
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:41,980
爸爸 你需要我帮你脱掉裙子吗
Hey, dad. You need any help out of that dress?

557
00:18:42,260 --> 00:18:43,200
除非你想看我
Not unless you want to see me

558
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:44,640
一丝不挂只穿着一个新年婴儿纸尿裤
in nothing but a baby new year's diaper.

559
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:45,740
那是你在发短信时
That was the big finish

560
00:18:45,740 --> 00:18:47,120
我要唱的歌的结尾重头戏
to the song you were texting through.

561
00:18:47,180 --> 00:18:49,540
我就收了一条短信 我看了大部分节目
Hey, I got one text. I saw most of the show --

562
00:18:49,540 --> 00:18:50,080
我们这就走了
We're leaving, okay?

563
00:18:50,080 --> 00:18:51,140
你能回桌子上
Could you just go to the table

564
00:18:51,140 --> 00:18:52,300
拿我的钥匙和包吗
and grab my keys and purse?

565
00:18:52,300 --> 00:18:53,127
好吧
Fine.

566
00:18:53,740 --> 00:18:55,080
你想聊聊吗
You want to talk about it?

567
00:18:55,100 --> 00:18:56,820
你到底能假扮几种医生
How many kinds of fake doctor are you?

568
00:18:57,160 --> 00:18:59,240
好了 到了揭晓今晚大奖的时刻了
Okay, time for the big award of the night,

569
00:18:59,360 --> 00:19:00,020
"年地经"奖[年度地产经纪]
The ROY...

570
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:01,560
我都不知道自己为什么生她的气
I don't even know why I'm mad at her.

571
00:19:01,560 --> 00:19:04,060
也许只是因为她整晚都显得很无聊
Probably just 'cause she was so bored all night.

572
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:05,680
也许你感觉自己不被她接纳
Maybe you're feeling rejected?

573
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:06,880
是我自己的错
It's my own fault.

574
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:07,780
我给了自己一个错误的希望
I built up this hope

575
00:19:07,780 --> 00:19:09,440
以为她会愿意追随我进入地产业
that she'd want to follow me into real estate.

576
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:10,420
菲尔·邓菲
...Phil Dunphy.

577
00:19:11,300 --> 00:19:12,460
她现在有自己的生活了
She's got her own life now.

578
00:19:12,460 --> 00:19:13,960
我只是不知道我们还能在哪里有联系
I just don't know where we connect anymore.

579
00:19:14,920 --> 00:19:15,320
你赢了
You won.

580
00:19:15,580 --> 00:19:16,720
-什么 -是啊
- What?! - Yeah.

581
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:17,940
扶我起来
Help me up!

582
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,020
我们都知道
As we all know,

583
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:22,560
菲尔今晚出了点小意外
Phil had a little accident tonight,

584
00:19:22,580 --> 00:19:23,640
但我们很乐意
but we're happy to accept

585
00:19:23,640 --> 00:19:24,600
-替他接受这个奖项 -等等 等等
- this award on his behalf. - Wait, wait, wait.

586
00:19:24,600 --> 00:19:25,380
等等 等等
Wait, w-w-w-w-wait!

587
00:19:25,380 --> 00:19:26,600
我来
I got this.

588
00:19:27,420 --> 00:19:28,980
大家好 我是
Hi. I'm, uh,

589
00:19:28,989 --> 00:19:30,840
我是海莉 菲尔的女儿
I'm haley, Phil's daughter.

590
00:19:30,840 --> 00:19:32,420
爸爸 你赢得了"年地经"
Dad, you won the ROY!

591
00:19:35,600 --> 00:19:38,180
你们都知道他是个出色的地产经纪
You all know him as an amazing realtor,

592
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:40,920
但我知道他还是世界上最棒的爸爸
but I know him as the world's greatest dad.

593
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:43,000
据我所知
As far as I'm concerned,

594
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:44,780
他也是年度最佳父亲
he's the dad of the year,

595
00:19:44,780 --> 00:19:45,540
"年爸爸"奖得主
the "DOY."

596
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:47,900
今晚真的很遗憾
It really is a shame

597
00:19:47,900 --> 00:19:49,820
你们没有听完他的完整演出
that you didn't hear the rest of his act tonight.

598
00:19:49,820 --> 00:19:52,214
但我有听过他排练
I-I heard him rehearsing it.

599
00:19:55,320 --> 00:19:57,020
你们哪位是J.J.·麦卡宾
Which one of you is J.J. McCubbin?

600
00:19:57,920 --> 00:20:00,100
快速问答 J.J.
Oh. Hey, quick question, J.J. --

601
00:20:00,220 --> 00:20:01,660
为什么一个好的抵押就像
Why is a great mortgage rate

602
00:20:01,660 --> 00:20:03,240
你老婆的床上表现
like your wife in bed?

603
00:20:03,240 --> 00:20:05,295
一个月一次还低利息[兴趣]
Once a month and low interest.

604
00:20:06,662 --> 00:20:08,340
你笑什么 斯基普·伍斯奴
What are you laughing at, Skip Woosnum?

605
00:20:08,340 --> 00:20:09,300
自从你加入海军后
You haven't seen a commission

606
00:20:09,300 --> 00:20:10,400
就没收过佣金了[服役]
since you joined the navy.

607
00:20:11,540 --> 00:20:12,720
她真是棒极了
She is killing it.

608
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:13,580
这才是我闺女
That's my girl.

609
00:20:13,620 --> 00:20:14,960
但我会在"海军"上加重语气
I would have hit the word "Navy" harder.

610
00:20:15,360 --> 00:20:17,660
还有什么 还有什么来着
What else? What else?

611
00:20:18,040 --> 00:20:19,680
玛格利特·福曼也来了
Oh! Margaret Furman's here.

612
00:20:19,680 --> 00:20:21,262
我要提醒一下她的男伴
Little heads-up to her date --

613
00:20:21,262 --> 00:20:24,134
她比房利美公司拥有更多资不抵债住房
She's been upside-down in more houses than Fannie Mae.

614
00:20:25,160 --> 00:20:27,860
或者说 房利一定会美
Or, in her case, Fannie definitely will.

615
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:31,080
我们都希望别人看到自己最好的一面
We all want people to think the best of us...

616
00:20:31,420 --> 00:20:33,300
所以有时我们会隐藏一些事
So sometimes we cover things up

617
00:20:33,300 --> 00:20:34,440
以保护自己
to protect ourselves.

618
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:38,960
但我们不必害怕
But we don't have to be afraid...

619
00:20:40,700 --> 00:20:43,440
因为真相永远是一件好事
Because the truth is always a good thing.

620
00:20:44,920 --> 00:20:46,940
真相让我们自由
The truth sets us free...

621
00:20:50,060 --> 00:20:51,140
让我们更亲近
...brings us closer.

622
00:20:52,360 --> 00:20:53,820
你想不想告诉我们
So, do you want to tell us

623
00:20:53,820 --> 00:20:55,600
乔的鞋怎么会穿错脚了呢
How Joe's shoes ended up on the wrong feet?

624
00:20:56,020 --> 00:20:58,780
看来小家伙学会了自己穿鞋
I guess the little guy knows how to put on his own shoes.

625
00:21:04,120 --> 00:21:05,980
开始吧 伙计 你能行
There you go, buddy. You got this.

626
00:21:06,220 --> 00:21:07,000
你在干什么
What are you doing?

627
00:21:07,260 --> 00:21:08,420
既然乔会走路了
Since Joe can walk now,

628
00:21:08,420 --> 00:21:09,880
我觉得他应该分担些家务了
I figured he should be doing a few chores.

629
00:21:09,880 --> 00:21:10,800
稳一点 大小伙
Steady, big guy!

630
00:21:11,100 --> 00:21:12,020
家务 什么样的
Chores? What kind of --

631
00:21:12,680 --> 00:21:13,420
他来了
There he is.

632
00:21:15,120 --> 00:21:15,520
好孩子
Attaboy!

633
00:21:15,520 --> 00:21:15,920
好孩子
Attaboy!

634
00:21:16,300 --> 00:21:18,180
啤酒 你疯了吗
A beer? Are you crazy?

635
00:21:18,180 --> 00:21:19,980
你去哪 你想来点吗
Where you going? You want some?

636
00:21:19,980 --> 00:21:20,720
他也可以给你拿
He'll bring it to you.

637
00:21:20,740 --> 00:21:22,640
我简直不敢相信你竟然教他做那种事
I can't believe that you're teaching him to do that.

638
00:21:22,640 --> 00:21:24,499
看完第二段再评论吧
Wait till you see part two.

639
00:21:25,020 --> 00:21:25,420
好孩子
Attaboy.

640
00:21:25,420 --> 00:21:28,880
放心吧 是我自己
Relax, it was me.
